WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.502
March Madness is upon us.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.436
Duke head coach
Mike Krzyzewski,

00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:05.939
is set to retire as perhaps

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.741
the greatest college basketball
coach of all time.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.177
And you must acknowledge
his greatness.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:15.848 line:0%
REPORTER:<i> The final home game
of Coach Mike Krzyzewski's
 Duke coaching career.</i>

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.651 line:0%
<i>This was the entry for the man,
 the myth, the legend.</i>

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:22.455 line:0%
REPORTER 2:<i> 96 former players
 came to support him.</i>

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.024 line:0%
<i> Jerry Seinfeld
and NBA commissioner Adam Silver</i>

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.259 line:0%
<i> were among those
 in the building.</i>

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.527 line:0%
I don't even know what to say.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.897 line:0%
It's like part
of my basketball life
is disappearing.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.399
Thank you, Coach K,
and go Duke.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:34.733
(SCOFFS) Please.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.002
You know what you didn't see
in that video?

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:42.041
A lot of Black people over 35.
We kind of hate that dude.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:46.813
We hate that he beat
every team Black people loved.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.249
Ten years ago,
if Duke would have played
the Ku Klux Klan,

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.053
we would have rooted
for a 0-0 tie.

00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:56.022
However, to much of the nation,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.157
Duke basketball was
like venture capital.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.293
Speaking with a manager,
bringing your dog to work.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.796
Symbolic of white excellence,

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.599
just like these
excellent white Duke alums,

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.467
<i>Richard Nixon, Richard Spencer,</i>

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.938
<i>and the man who wears his heart
on his hairline, Stephen Miller.</i>

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:16.542
Coach K brought those excellent
vibes to Durham in 1980.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.944
Just listen to how he talks
about their recruiting.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:23.649
What Duke does is it gives me--
it limits some of my recruiting

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:28.254
because not every youngster
can get into Duke.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:33.125
And that doesn't mean that kids
who don't make it at Duke
are worse or better.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:37.163
It's just that schools are
for different kids.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.967
Doesn't sound like
he was recruiting the kids
from Rosa Parks High School.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:45.672
Let me be clear,
Coach K's legacy is built on

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.606
society's perception
of whiteness,

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:51.644
the idea that
his players overcame
their physical deficiencies,

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:55.614
that they were harder working,
smarter, not as athletic.

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.217
Being good made Coach K a star.

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.587
Being better than us
made him a legend.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.390
And that's not
Coach K being racist.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.595
But the rest of you...
(CHUCKLES) I don't know.

00:02:09.394 --> 00:02:11.063
So let me take it back to 1980.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.100
The rising tide of Blackness
in college basketball

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.002
was a threat to the whole game.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.906
That year,
the Louisville Cardinals
won their first championship.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.809
<i> Some people called them
 the Blackbirds.</i>

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:28.448
<i> Yes, it only took
a half-Black roster to get
a racist nickname back then.</i>

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.750
Not quite the one drop rule,

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.885
but damn if it don't
feel the same.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.622
Anyway, soon after,
John Thompson's Georgetown

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:40.426
established itself as a power,
Black power.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:45.197
Every single player
on their 1984 Championship team
was Black.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:47.733
<i> If somebody would've
called them the Blackbirds,</i>

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.235
<i> I would've understood.</i>

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:54.139
But in 1986,
Duke lost to Louisville
in the National Championship.

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:57.076
Check out how the
<i>Chicago Tribune</i> felt about that.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.055
They really must've thought
Black players couldn't read

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.689
if they printed that shit.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:14.393
I mean, it's not like
white sports fans had nothing
to be proud of.

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:17.163
The best player in the NBA
was Larry Bird.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.365
Quarterbacks were still
supposed to be white.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:22.468
And the heavyweight champions
of the world were these guys!

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:27.073
But college basketball
seemed on the brink
of eternal darkness.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.910
That's when Coach K pulled up
with the Caucasian Avengers.

00:03:31.343 --> 00:03:34.113
<i>And their Captain America
 was this guy.</i>

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.415
Now, before you say anything,

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:40.286
we're not erasing
Johnny Dawkins, Grant Hill,
and other Black Devils.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.521
But Christian Laettner
was so white,

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.590
he got caught
stepping on somebody

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.026
and didn't even get thrown out
of the game.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:51.264
BOBBY HURLEY:<i> It was symbolic
 of why some people
 didn't like Christian,</i>

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:55.467 line:0%
you know, in terms of
him willing to cross the line

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.336
<i> and do something
 a little bit arrogant.</i>

00:03:58.003 --> 00:04:00.206
It was just a little love tap
on his chest.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.874
Asshole.

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:08.046
Duke beat every team
Black folks loved
from 1986 to '92.

00:04:08.146 --> 00:04:11.417
<i>Georgetown, Arkansas, UNLV.</i>

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:15.221
And the one program that felt
the most like ours,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.156
<i> Michigan's Fab Five.</i>

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.425
<i> Look at these
 cool motherfuckers.</i>

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:23.562
<i>Black socks, long shorts,
 pristine edge-ups.</i>

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.432
Well, Coach K
and the Supercuts all-stars

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.868
kicked they fresh asses
repeatedly.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.904
No wonder Jalen Rose
was salty about it.

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:35.341
JALEN ROSE:<i> Schools like Duke
didn't recruit players like me.</i>

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:39.112 line:0%
I feel like they only
recruited Black players
that were Uncle Toms.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.080
Too far, Jalen.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.785
But to be fair, it seemed to me
that the press wasn't just
rooting for Duke,

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:48.287
they were standing up for them
along the way.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:51.423
CBS REPORTER:
<i>I'm sure that the UNLV players
 are gaining some respect</i>

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.158
<i> for the courage
of the Duke players as well.</i>

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:54.994
CBS REPORTER 2:
<i>Neither team backing away,</i>

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:57.296
<i>and that's an important thing
 to consider</i>

00:04:57.396 --> 00:04:58.564
<i>when you're playing Georgetown.</i>

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:00.233 line:0%
<i> They play you tough
 and physical,</i>

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.568 line:0%
<i> and the only way is
to look 'em straight in the eye</i>

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:04.336 line:0%
<i> and say,
"We'll play that way too."</i>

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:06.672 line:0%
<i> I mean, that's just
the way it is athletically.</i>

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:10.943 line:0%
<i> I don't think anybody
should make any great, big
 headline deal out of it.</i>

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.579
BOB COSTAS:<i> The Fab Five
against America's finest,</i>

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:14.747
<i> coming up next.</i>

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.384
America's finest?!
Who are they, the Durham PD?

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.119
Now, remember.

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.688
At this point,
a lot of folks loved Duke

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.556
as much as they hated hip hop,

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:27.059
which was taking over
everywhere,

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:29.295
except college basketball.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:33.566
Until now, this was
the closest rap had gotten
to college ball.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.402
<i> ♪ 'Cause it's basketball
 Mr. Kurtis Blow ♪</i>

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.872
<i>♪ They're playing basketball ♪</i>

00:05:40.605 --> 00:05:44.510
<i>♪ We love that basketball ♪</i>

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.745
But some of those
iconic Black teams

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:50.016
started bringing the culture
right onto the basketball court
with 'em.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.417
But not Duke.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:56.055
Coach K's kids
didn't break it down,
break beats, or breakdance.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.357
You'd scratch a record
at Danny Ferry's house,

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:00.359
and you'd owe him
a new<i> Toto</i> album,

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:02.962
which is the closest
Africa got to Duke

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.664
until Luol Deng showed up.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.332
Either way,
Coach K was claiming,

00:06:07.432 --> 00:06:10.970
"All I do is win"
way before DJ Khaled.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.174
And yeah,
Duke had a down year in 1995.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:19.278
But that got Coach K
to recruit outside of his usual
young Republicans.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:22.381
He brought in some of the most
talented teams he ever had,

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:24.817
and they got really good again.

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:29.488
<i> But then, in 1999,
for the first time ever at Duke,</i>

00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:31.390
<i>those guys left school early</i>

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.826
<i> and took all their swag
 with them to the NBA.</i>

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:39.799
In 2006, Coach K had figured out
how to go from Steve Urkel
to Stefan Urquelle.

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:42.901
He became the coach
of USA Basketball.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.838
That got
all the cool kid's attention.

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.673
LEBRON JAMES:
<i>You know, I love Coach K.</i>

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.274
<i> I love playing for him,
 I love talking to him</i>

00:06:49.374 --> 00:06:51.077 line:0%
on off days
and during practices.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:54.246 line:0%
And, you know,
I've been blessed,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.115
<i> with me not having
the ability to go to college</i>

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:57.516
<i> coming straight
 out of high school,</i>

00:06:57.649 --> 00:06:58.584
<i> to have a college coach.</i>

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:01.654
LeBron said he didn't have
the ability to go to college

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.355
like he couldn't read
or something.

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:07.393
Not because he was
too smart to pass up
a 90-million-dollar Nike deal.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:12.398
Anyway, the point is that
the kids who didn't know nothing
about no Christian Laettner

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.700
knew about players on Team USA,

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.036
like Kobe, Kevin Durant,
and LeBron James.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:23.508
And now, somehow,
the name Mike Krzyzewski

00:07:23.608 --> 00:07:26.412
rings out in the streets
like Nicky Barnes.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.981
DUKE PLAYER:<i> Coach K get love
 in the streets.</i>

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:32.251
<i> So it don't matter
if we in Manhattan or Harlem,</i>

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.688
they know Coach K, man.
It's crazy.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:38.290
Think about how crazy that is.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.293
In the '80s, parents from Duke
wouldn't let their kids

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.295
get within 40 acres of Harlem.

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:47.066
Now, this team looks like
the kids who sell you candy
on the train.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:51.169
The all-academic Duke team
that everybody talked about

00:07:51.269 --> 00:07:53.172
was full of one-and-doners.

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:54.673
But it's funny.

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:57.576
Hardly anyone called
Krzyzewski a hypocrite.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.446
'Cause when he did it,
that was just the game

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:02.647
because he was the game.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:05.284 line:0%
Are you a supported
of this one-and-done rule?

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.552 line:0%
It doesn't make any difference
if you're supportive of it.

00:08:07.652 --> 00:08:09.188 line:0%
We have no control over it.

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:11.256 line:0%
What you have to do,
like you have to do in business,

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:12.191 line:0%
is adapt.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.293
And adapt he did.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.997
Because Black culture
did eventually take over
college basketball.

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:20.232
But I'll be honest,

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:24.537
college basketball was better
when Duke was the official team
of white America.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:28.007
Every game felt like
one of those episodes
of<i> Family Feud.</i>

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:31.643
Think about basketball
like the name Tyrone.

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:35.848
After a while, white folks just
let us keep it for ourselves.

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:39.551
But you know some folks
won't let us have nothing.

00:08:39.751 --> 00:08:42.655
And for four decades,
a lot of fans felt like

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:47.326
Coach K was the one person
who just couldn't let us have
this one thing.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:51.964
It all felt, like, personal,
even if it wasn't.

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:55.333
So believe me when I say,
sincerely,

00:08:55.767 --> 00:08:57.837
happy retirement, Coach K.

00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:01.707
No one has been wishing
for this day longer than us.

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:05.077
So to commemorate
the real legacy of Coach K,

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.881
we decided to give him
his very own museum exhibit.

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:10.516
Check it out.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:16.022
<i>To help the Black community
process Coach K's 42-year
 reign of terror,</i>

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:19.891
<i>we opened The Boys in Blue:
Coach K's March Across America,</i>

00:09:20.225 --> 00:09:23.629
<i> an exhibit at the
Schomburg Center for Research
in Black Culture in Harlem.</i>

00:09:24.129 --> 00:09:27.466
<i> All day,
we led the public on tours
through our many exhibits,</i>

00:09:27.566 --> 00:09:32.171
<i> highlighting Coach K's
destruction of our beautiful
Black college basketball teams.</i>

00:09:32.271 --> 00:09:35.141
This section of the exhibit
is called Trail of Sneers.

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:37.376
Look at this picture right now.
What do you see?

00:09:37.709 --> 00:09:40.580
A coach talking to a ref
or a Karen talking to a cop?

00:09:41.813 --> 00:09:42.815
Same vibes.

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.550
Sir, I see you.
I see your face is scrunching.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.585
You've seen these faces before.

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:49.355
-And were they
bringing you good news?
-Never.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:51.557
-Were they
bringing you positivity?
-Never.

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.559
-Were they uplifting you?
-Never.

00:09:53.659 --> 00:09:55.294
I want you to look at this one
right here.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:56.928
What do you get when you look
at this picture?

00:09:57.028 --> 00:09:59.498
A lot of anger in his eyes.

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:02.234
How he feels about himself
and others.

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.770
-So you see self-hate.
-Mm-hmm.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.339
The anger's coming from within.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:09.508
-That man right there
stole my dreams.
-Talk to me.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:12.244
I used to play
high school basketball
with Jamal Mashburn,

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:13.545
and I lost to him.

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:15.714
-Are you still friends
with Jamal Mashburn?
-MUSEUMGOER: Absolutely.

00:10:15.814 --> 00:10:18.083
-Is he still troubled
by what happened?
-Absolutely.

00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:20.819
If you could express
your feelings about Coach K
in one word,

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:22.120
what would that word be?

00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:24.256
-Terror.
-TOUR GUIDE: Terror?

00:10:25.423 --> 00:10:26.792
I think that about sums it up.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:28.661
Let's move on
to the next section, everybody.

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:31.230
JONES:<i> He wasn't
the only one Coach K terrified.</i>

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.867
<i>Our exhibit also showcased
the nightmarish illustrations</i>

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:38.070
<i>the children of Detroit drew
after Duke defeated the Fab Five</i>

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:41.206
<i> in the 1992 NCAA
 Championship game.</i>

00:10:41.606 --> 00:10:44.043
As a native
of Detroit, Michigan,

00:10:44.376 --> 00:10:46.344
this is only giving me PTSD.

00:10:46.444 --> 00:10:48.146
So you saw the game
that these kids saw?

00:10:48.613 --> 00:10:51.583
-And I was that age.
-The city was down altogether.

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:56.255
I'm sure the water
got a little dirtier
after this defeat.

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:58.090
That's Flint.

00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:01.360
My bad, my bad.

00:11:01.827 --> 00:11:04.463
JONES:<i> Dozens of artefacts
tell the stories of Black trauma</i>

00:11:04.697 --> 00:11:06.164
<i>like Aminu Timberlake's jersey</i>

00:11:06.264 --> 00:11:09.001
<i> that Christian Laettner
stomped on with his punk ass,</i>

00:11:09.834 --> 00:11:11.637
<i>Coach K's single game salary,</i>

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:15.240
<i> and the salaries
 of every Duke player
 from 1980 to present,</i>

00:11:15.741 --> 00:11:18.811
<i>and the embarrassing linchpins
 to Coach K's success.</i>

00:11:19.244 --> 00:11:20.846
TOUR GUIDE:<i> The next section
 of the exhibit is called</i>

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:22.681
<i>The Wall of Unimpressive Whites.</i>

00:11:22.915 --> 00:11:24.783
It was these goofy
white athletes

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:27.953
that were out there
beating our amazing

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.356
Black college basketball teams.

00:11:30.456 --> 00:11:31.990
And of course, Shelden Williams.

00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:35.394
He is not white, but he is...
white by association.

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:38.831
Look at this guy! He looks
like<i> Top Gun's</i> co-pilot.

00:11:38.931 --> 00:11:40.132
-What was his name?
-Goose.

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:42.435
TOUR GUIDE: Goose!
This Goose-looking motherfucker

00:11:43.101 --> 00:11:44.670
beating all our teams.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:45.904
And that's wrong!

00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:48.240
-Y'all ready for
the next section of the exhibit?
-ALL: Yes.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.375
I need some water. I'm ti--
I'm getting pissed off.

00:11:50.642 --> 00:11:53.412
JONES:<i> And I get it,
these corn-fed, cop calling,</i>

00:11:53.645 --> 00:11:56.348
<i>cul-de-sac dwelling Caucasoids,
 and Sheldon,</i>

00:11:56.848 --> 00:11:58.817
<i> had shattered the dreams
 of our heroes.</i>

00:11:59.251 --> 00:12:02.254
<i> Thankfully, our
Alter of the NCAA Dead Homies</i>

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:04.323
<i> gave patrons a chance
 to pay their respects.</i>

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:06.425
Chris Webber,
that was my dude, man.

00:12:07.426 --> 00:12:10.495
I had the--
I had the black socks.

00:12:10.729 --> 00:12:12.230
Anybody-- Anybody have
the black socks?

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.832
-Y'all have the black socks?
-I had the black socks.

00:12:13.899 --> 00:12:15.134
TOUR GUIDE:
Remember the black socks?

00:12:15.467 --> 00:12:18.536
JONES:<i> But their pain
 was nothing compared to
 what some have endured.</i>

00:12:18.803 --> 00:12:21.440
And now, we've reached the
Jalen Rose part of our exhibit.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.742
Ladies and gentlemen,
Jalen Rose.

00:12:24.743 --> 00:12:28.980
A true survivor of Coach K's
march across America.

00:12:29.815 --> 00:12:34.219
I'm O-and-four against Coach K.
He beat me each time.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:40.726
Even once after my uncle passed
and they came to Ann Arbor.

00:12:41.226 --> 00:12:43.662
I had a patch on my jersey
and everything.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:45.464
It still didn't matter.

00:12:45.564 --> 00:12:46.799
This is not fiction.

00:12:47.099 --> 00:12:49.234
This ain't no wax figure.
This a real one right here.

00:12:49.334 --> 00:12:52.637
I once dribbled the ball across
half court against Bobby Hurley.

00:12:53.571 --> 00:12:56.408
And he just fell for no reason,
and they called a charge.

00:12:56.475 --> 00:12:57.709
Goddamn flopper.

00:12:57.976 --> 00:12:59.178
Who's Bobby Hurley?

00:12:59.645 --> 00:13:01.980
A miniature point guard
for the Duke Blue Devils.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:02.947
Small man.

00:13:03.047 --> 00:13:05.284
Are those really his shorts?

00:13:05.784 --> 00:13:09.889
They are.
We wore extra baggy shorts.

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:13.859
Bobby Hurley chose
a kid's medium.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.762
Too much thigh for my eye.

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:18.130
JONES:<i> Damn right.</i>

00:13:18.664 --> 00:13:20.833
<i>And we shouldn't allow ourselves
 to be terrorized</i>

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:24.503
<i> by these creamy-thighed
 OshKosh B'gosh Devils.</i>

00:13:24.936 --> 00:13:26.705
<i> These Duke athletes
 aren't monsters,</i>

00:13:27.038 --> 00:13:30.175
<i> they're suckers led by
a five-foot ten-inch tyrant</i>

00:13:30.275 --> 00:13:33.078
<i> that we, as a community,
 have overcome.</i>

00:13:33.712 --> 00:13:36.247
<i>Our day had come to an end,
 but of course,</i>

00:13:36.348 --> 00:13:38.384
<i> no Black history museum
 would be complete</i>

00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:41.920
<i> without a cool down area
 to process our emotions.</i>

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:47.926
Breathe in,
and return to the real world
with a renewed sense of self.

00:13:48.427 --> 00:13:52.331
And always remember
that Coach K collected
over 40 years of victories,

00:13:52.898 --> 00:13:57.169
but Danny Green
still put his balls
on Greg Paulus' forehead.

00:13:58.437 --> 00:13:59.438
Keep hope alive.

00:13:59.538 --> 00:14:03.876
♪ (PATRIOTIC MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

